The '''Multi-Troop Transport (MTT)''' was a heavily [[armor]]ed [[repulsorlift]] [[transport]] vehicle manufactured by [[Baktoid Armor Workshop]] and used by both the [[Trade Federation]] during their [[Invasion of Naboo]] and later the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] to transport [[B1-series battle droid]]s before and during the [[Clone Wars]]. During the Clone Wars, it was used to transport [[B2-series super battle droid]]s.

==Characteristics==
Manufactured by [[Baktoid Armor Workshop]] for the [[Trade Federation]] and later the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], the Multi-Troop [[Transport]] was a heavy, broad-shouldered, snub-nosed [[repulsorlift]] vehicle designed to transport [[battle droid]]s into combat.<ref name="Rise" /> Massive, lumbering, imposing vehicles, the 35.94 [[meter]] long and 10.45 meter tall<ref name="Databank" /> MTT was considered a [[troop carrier]], a [[tank]], and a siege ram.<ref name="Rise" /> It was difficult to stop at a maximum speed of thirty-one [[Kilometer per hour|kilometers per hour]],<ref name="ESOV" /> and when compared to the [[Armored Assault Tank Mk I|Armored Assault Tank]] also used by the Federation and Confederacy, it was extremely capable in its role. For defensive purposes, the Multi-Troop Transport was armed with a pair of forward-mounted antipersonnel twin [[blaster cannon]]s. They were additionally equipped with close-ranged [[sensor]]s.<ref name="Rise" />

[[File:MTTopenforbusiness-SWE.png|thumb|left|250px|An MTT deploying its battle droids]]
With its hulking forward [[hull]], sloping front end, and small aft hull, the MTT had a vaguely elephantine silhouette.<ref name="Rise" /> A small [[armor]]ed [[cockpit]] was mounted atop the towering hull, directly above a large, thick, circular hatch, where two [[OOM pilot battle droid]]s served as the vehicle's operators. These two [[pilot droid]]s directed the vehicle according to the instructions received from a [[Lucrehulk-class battleship|''Lucrehulk''-class Battleship]]. One of the [[pilot]]s would serve as an [[engineer]] and a [[gunner]].<ref name="Complete Vehicles2018">[[Star Wars: Complete Vehicles (2018)|''Star Wars: Complete Vehicles'' (2018)]]</ref> Much of the interior was given over to the hydraulically powered [[droid]] deployment rack,<ref name="USW" /> a long rotating assembly that carried a total of one hundred and twelve deactivated [[B1-series battle droid]]s.<ref name="Episode I" />

In order to deploy the droids, the MTT was required to cease movement, open the hatch, and extend the rack, where the droids were then quickly deployed and activated, creating an instant [[infantry]] formation.<ref name="Rise" /> Another variant of MTT deployment rack dropped its robotic soldiers from a few meters off the ground, falling into their battle-ready configuration<ref name="JediSurvivor" /> rather than taking the time to rise from a compact form.<ref name="Episode I" /> However, the quicker deployment rack held less droids.<ref name="JediSurvivor" /> A maximum of twelve [[B2-series super battle droid]]s could be stored in such a rack.<ref name="Massacre" /> A mix of several B1s, B2s, and [[BX-series droid commando]]s could be stored on such a rack as well.<ref name="JediSurvivor" />

==Role==
{{Quote|My spies tell me those transports carry treasure.|Cham Syndulla, on how Wat Tambor used MTTs during the battle of Ryloth|<ref name="Liberty on Ryloth">{{TCW|Liberty on Ryloth}}</ref>}}
Multi-Troop Transports were utilized by the Trade Federation, and later the Confederacy of Independent Systems, to deposit over a hundred battle droid infantry troops into the thick of combat on battlefields. Assisted by an orbital ''Lucrehulk''-class Battleship, which sent an activation signal to the droids, the MTT deployed its stowed soldiers into their battle-ready [[humanoid]] configuration.<ref name="Databank" />

[[File:Trade_Federation_Droid_Army.png|thumb|right|280px|MTTs as part of the invasion force on Naboo]]
MTTs were typically supported by phalanxes of Armored Assault Tanks, which cleared the path ahead to allow the troop transports to deploy their units,<ref name="SWE MTT">{{SWE|technology|mtt|MTT}}</ref> although MTTs were also used to support front lines and front ranks comprised of AATs.<ref name="SWCL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> Multi-Troop Transports were themselves deployed from within [[C-9979 landing craft]],<ref name="Databank Landing Ship">{{Databank|trade-federation-landing-ship|Trade Federation Landing Ship}}</ref> which carried eleven MTTs each.<ref name="SWCL" />

==History==
{{Quote|Looks like more reinforcements. A small droid convoy leading a Multi-Troop Transport.|Saw Gerrera, to his sister and fellow [[Onderon rebels|Onderon rebel]] [[Steela Gerrera]]|<ref name="The Soft War">{{TCW|The Soft War}}</ref>}}
Numerous Multi-Troop Transports were deployed from landing craft during the [[Invasion of Naboo]]. Disgorged into the [[planet]]'s [[swamp]]s, MTTs bulldozed anything in their path, from [[tree]]s to native life-forms,<ref name="Episode I" /> and thirty-three of the large transports ultimately assisted in the occupation of [[Theed]].<ref name="SWCL" /> They were later part of the [[Trade Federation Droid Army]] sent to [[Battle of Naboo|confront]] the [[Gungan Grand Army]] on the [[Great Grass Plains]]. When the [[Gungan]]s' [[deflector shield]]s proved strong enough to withstand bombardment from Armored Assault Tanks, a line of MTTs deployed their B1-series battle droids to walk through the energy wall and engage the Gungans in single combat.<ref name="Episode I" /> The MTTs remained a fearsome presence throughout the battle, some closing in to trap the Gungan army, and once the [[deflector shield generator]]s were destroyed, many Gungans became vulnerable to the transports' laser fire.<ref name="SWCL" />

[[File:Dowutin_SWC.jpg|thumb|left|260px|Dowutin Hunters operated Multi-Troop Transports during the Galactic Civil War]]
MTTs were used by the Confederacy of Independent Systems during the [[Clone Wars]], transporting infantry troops to numerous battlefields, and many were painted in Confederacy livery.<ref name="Databank" />

By [[9 BBY]],<ref name="SurvivorDate">{{JediSurvivorDate}}</ref> the [[Bedlam Raiders]] on [[Koboh]] had an MTT in their possession within one of their outposts. The transport carried six B1-series battle droids, two B2-series super battle droids, and four [[BX-series droid commando]]s.<ref name="JediSurvivor" />

{{Gamemechanics|Star Wars Jedi: Survivor|canon=1}}
In 9 BBY,<ref name="SurvivorDate" /> [[Jedi Knight]] [[Cal Kestis]] encountered the Bedlam Raiders' MTT and destroyed the droids carried inside of it.<ref name="JediSurvivor" />
{{Endgame}}

Multi-Troop Transports were used by the [[Dowutin Hunter]]s, [[Mercenary|mercenaries]] active during the [[Galactic Civil War]] who fought for both the [[Galactic Empire]] and the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]. These transports were modified, donning a predominantly green and yellow [[color]] scheme likened to that of their Dowutin operators.<ref name="Commander" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Deactivated-B1s-in-MTT.png|thumb|right|250px|B1 battle droids kept in an MTT in the ''Battlefront II'' trailer]]
The MTT first appeared in the [[1999]] film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']], the first installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[prequel trilogy]].<ref name="Episode I" />

The [[Encyclopedia (StarWars.com)|Starwars.com Encyclopedia]] listed the length of this vehicle as 25.94 [[meter]]s, while the newer [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] lists it as 35.94 meters.

The design of the [[rail jet]] cars inside the ''[[Malevolence]]'' drew inspiration from the MTT.<ref name="Destroy Malevolence Ep Guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/destroy-malevolence-episode-guide|text="Destroy Malevolence" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref>

The MTT also appears in ''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]'', in which the player, if they are part of the Separatist team, is able to pilot the vehicle in the game's Naboo and [[Kashyyyk]] levels. If the player is not inside the vehicle, they are tasked with defending the MTT from Republic [[ion cannon]]s.<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref>

